onMouseOut="nd();">
Plin. 18.280</A>.


<P CLASS="ivy">❦</P>


	<P CLASS="justify">
	<A CLASS="note" ID="note8" HREF="
E/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis*.html#ref8
"onMouseOver="return Ebox(INARRAY,BackRef,WIDTH,175)"
onMouseOut="nd();">8</A>
<I>cf.</I> Arat. 73 f.<!--</A>ARATUS-->


<P CLASS="ivy">❦</P>


	<P CLASS="justify">
	<A CLASS="note" ID="note9" HREF="
E/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis*.html#ref9
"onMouseOver="return Ebox(INARRAY,BackRef,WIDTH,175)"
onMouseOut="nd();">9</A>
<SPAN LANG="el" CLASS="Greek">τὸν ὑπογ. τρόπον</SPAN> seems to mean the same as the Aristotelian <SPAN LANG="el" CLASS="Greek">τὸν ὑφηγημένον τρόπον</SPAN>, <I>e.g.</I> <I>Eth. Nic.</I> 2.7.9. The rendering 'the following method' would however suit the context.


<P CLASS="ivy">❦</P>


	<P CLASS="justify">
	<A CLASS="note" ID="note10" HREF="
E/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis*.html#ref10
"onMouseOver="return Ebox(INARRAY,BackRef,WIDTH,175)"
onMouseOut="nd();">10</A>
<SPAN LANG="el" CLASS="Greek">ἀνέχῃ</SPAN> conj. Sch.


<P CLASS="ivy">❦</P>


	<P CLASS="justify">
