E/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis*.html#25
"onMouseOver="return Ebox(INARRAY,5,WIDTH,140)"
onMouseOut="nd();">25</A>,
	<A HREF="
E/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis*.html#42
"onMouseOver="return Ebox(INARRAY,5,WIDTH,140)"
onMouseOut="nd();">
42</A>, <A HREF="
E/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis*.html#54
"onMouseOver="return Ebox(INARRAY,5,WIDTH,140)"
onMouseOut="nd();">54</A>.


<P CLASS="ivy">❦</P>


	<P CLASS="justify">
	<A CLASS="note" ID="note20" HREF="
E/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis*.html#ref20
"onMouseOver="return Ebox(INARRAY,BackRef,WIDTH,175)"
onMouseOut="nd();">20</A>
<I>i.e.</I> refuses to light properly. The appearance seems to be that described
	<A HREF="
https://www.hs-augsburg.de/~harsch/Chronologia/Lsante01/Vergilius/ver_ge01.html
	"TARGET="offsite"
onMouseOver="return Ebox(EClickHere+'Book 1<BR>of the Georgics'+Lat2+LatSearch+'oleum</SPAN>',WIDTH,195)"
onMouseOut="nd();">
Verg. <I>Georg.</I> 1.391
	</A>
(<SPAN LANG="la" CLASS="Latin">scintillare oleum</SPAN>). In the same passage <SPAN LANG="la" CLASS="Latin">putres concrescere fungos</SPAN> perhaps illustrates the comparison of the snuff to millet-seed above.


<P CLASS="ivy">❦</P>


	<P CLASS="justify">
	<A CLASS="note" ID="note21" HREF="
E/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis*.html#ref21
