<P CLASS="ivy">❦</P>


	<P CLASS="justify a0">
	<A CLASS="note" ID="note73" HREF="
E/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis*.html#ref73
"onMouseOver="return Ebox(INARRAY,BackRef,WIDTH,175)"
onMouseOut="nd();">73</A>
The 'figure' (giving points of the compass) has not been preserved. Arist. <I>Meteor.</I> describes such a figure (<SPAN LANG="el" CLASS="Greek">ὑπογραφή</SPAN>), which may be reconstructed thus:—

<TABLE CLASS="basicS white image">
	<TR><TD><IMG TITLE="" CLASS="basicS" SRC="
Images/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis/diagram_of_the_winds*.jpg
		" ALT="
[A diagram of a circle divided into eight equal wedges by four diameters: it is a diagram of the winds as viewed by Aristotle, with North at the top. The N wind is marked Boreas; the NE Kaikias, the E Apeliotes, the SW Euros, the S Notos, the SW Lips, the W Zephyros, the NW Argestes and alternately Olympias and Skiros. In addition, a diameter is drawn with a NNW wind Thraskias and a SSE Phoinikias; and finally, a radius with the NNE wind Meses.]
	"></TD></TR>
</TABLE>

	<P CLASS="i1 b0 a0 justify" ID="p415x">
Arist. does not seem to distinguish <SPAN LANG="el" CLASS="Greek">βορέας</SPAN> and <SPAN LANG="el" CLASS="Greek">ἀπαρκτίας</SPAN>: his <SPAN LANG="el" CLASS="Greek">θρασκίας</SPAN> is T.'s <SPAN LANG="el" CLASS="Greek">θρακίας</SPAN>: his eight principal winds (in red<A CLASS="comment"
onMouseOver="return Ebox('The Loeb edition has '+SearchF+'underlined'+CloseF+';<BR>taking advantage of the Web, I colorized the diagram.')"
onMouseOut="nd();">º</A> in diagram) correspond to those represented on the famous Tower of the Winds at Athens, built about two hundred years later.


<P CLASS="ivy">❦</P>


	<P CLASS="justify">
	<A CLASS="note" ID="note74" HREF="
E/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis*.html#ref74
"onMouseOver="return Ebox(INARRAY,BackRef,WIDTH,175)"
onMouseOut="nd();">74</A>
<I>cf.</I> Arist. l.c.


<P CLASS="ivy">❦</P>


	<P CLASS="justify">
	<A CLASS="note" ID="note75" HREF="
E/Roman/Texts/Theophrastus/De_signis*.html#ref75
"onMouseOver="return Ebox(INARRAY,BackRef,WIDTH,175)"
onMouseOut="nd();">75</A>
	<A HREF="
L/Roman/Texts/Pliny_the_Elder/2*.html#128
	"TARGET="Pliny"
onMouseOver="return Ebox(INARRAY,Pliny,WIDTH,205)"
onMouseOut="nd();">
Plin. 2.128</A>.


